From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: ROG5 apply video-mode perf votes before the encoders start

drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables() enables the CRTC, then the
encoders; dpu_core_perf_crtc_update() only runs in atomic_flush afterwards.
The INTF timing engine itself starts in handle_post_kickoff, after the CTL
flush (so after atomic_flush), not in the encoder enable: the encoder and
pipeline configuration (CTL, mixers, INTF, DP stream clocks) is written on
the previous, possibly low, bus/clock votes, but the first scanout already
runs on the new ones.

Apply the new performance state in dpu_crtc_enable() for CRTCs driving a
video-mode encoder, before the encoders are enabled. This is a cheap early
vote, not a proven fix: the r180 case this was written for (USB-C HDMI hub,
1080p60, DSI panel off: underrun on every frame even after the votes were
raised, until the next modeset, then 0/314) most likely was the colour-management
resource reassignment fixed by 0131/0132 (the GAMMA_LUT commit after the
first modeset moved the pipeline to other mixers without a modeset), not
the vote timing. (Text and comment corrected 2026-09-30; code unchanged.)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c	2026-09-29 15:38:28.260808836 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_crtc.c	2026-09-29 15:38:28.274383127 +0200
@@ -1309,6 +1309,16 @@
 	trace_dpu_crtc_enable(DRMID(crtc), true, dpu_crtc);
 	dpu_crtc->enabled = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * The encoders are enabled (configured) after the CRTC, before
+	 * atomic_flush applies the votes computed in atomic_check; the INTF
+	 * timing engine starts after the CTL flush. Apply the new performance
+	 * state before the encoders are configured (a cheap early vote; the
+	 * "underrun until the next modeset" seen on DP: see 0131/0132).
+	 */
+	if (request_bandwidth)
+		dpu_core_perf_crtc_update(crtc, 1);
+
 	if (!old_crtc_state->self_refresh_active) {
 		drm_for_each_encoder_mask(encoder, crtc->dev, crtc->state->encoder_mask)
 			dpu_encoder_assign_crtc(encoder, crtc);
